<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  nav step 5: a test world built specifically to exercise the frontier-aware
  tunnel-navigation capability (see
  docs/work-docs/nav/step05_frontier_tunnel_navigation.md) - a real, concrete
  case of the limitation that work solves: emap's UAV maps the world from
  directly overhead, so a structure that occludes the ground from above (a
  culvert, tunnel, or roofed passage) leaves everything underneath it
  permanently `is_valid=False`, no matter how thoroughly the surrounding
  area gets scanned. Without frontier mode, that reads as a solid wall to
  the planner - here it is deliberately made the ONLY route between the UGV's
  start point and its goal, so a live run either proves the capability works
  or clearly fails trying.

  Physics/scene/GUI/sensor plugin boilerplate is copied from
  worlds/room_maze.world (itself emap's own already-proven Ignition Fortress
  template) - nothing new needed there, including the z=500 light pose (see
  that file's own docstring for the real depth-camera-misreads-a-light bug
  this avoids).

  --- Layout ---
  One room, x in [-6, 6], y in [-4, 4], standard 2.5m-tall/0.15m-thick walls
  (same construction as room_maze.world's own walls). A partition wall at
  x=0 splits it into "room A" (x<0, the UGV's start side) and "room B" (x>0,
  the goal side), but the partition does NOT span the full width - it stops
  at y=+/-0.7, leaving a 1.4m-wide gap. That gap is filled, not left open,
  by a semi-cylindrical tunnel (see the 'tunnel' model below) whose hollow
  interior is the only way through - the partition wall's two segments and
  the tunnel's own arch meet flush at y=+/-0.7, so there is no way to walk
  from room A to room B without physically passing through the tunnel's
  interior at ground level.

  --- The tunnel model ---
  A true SDF primitive for "hollow half-cylinder" doesn't exist, so - same
  "self-authored from primitive boxes, no mesh" approach emap's
  construction_site.world building_frame model already used - the arch is
  approximated with 7 flat box segments, each tangent to a circle of radius
  0.7m at its own segment's midpoint angle, extruded 1.5m along X (the
  tunnel's own axis - the direction a robot actually drives through it).
  Left OPEN at both ends (x=-0.75 and x=+0.75) on purpose - those are the
  tunnel's two mouths.

  The math (worked out once, then baked in as literal numbers below - see
  the per-segment pose comments): for N=7 segments spanning a semicircle
  (180 degrees) of radius R=0.7m, segment i's midpoint angle is
  theta_i = (i + 0.5) * (180/7) degrees; each segment's local Y/Z position
  is (R*cos(theta_i), R*sin(theta_i)) (theta measured from the +Y axis
  toward +Z, so theta=0 is the ground-level mouth on the +Y side, theta=90
  is the very top of the arch, theta=180 is the ground-level mouth on the
  -Y side); each segment is rolled (rotated about its own local X axis, the
  tunnel's length axis) by (theta_i - 90 degrees) so its flat face sits
  tangent to the circle at that point, with its "width" axis lying along
  the arc. Segment width is the chord length for that arc slice
  (2*R*sin(dtheta/2)) scaled up ~12% so adjacent segments overlap slightly
  rather than leaving a seam a depth camera could see a sliver of true
  floor through.

  --- Start/goal visual markers ---
  Two non-colliding markers (visual-only links, no <collision> at all - so
  they cannot be mistaken for real obstacles by anything, camera or lidar)
  mark the UGV's spawn point (green) and the nav goal (red), so a human
  watching the GUI can immediately see both without cross-referencing launch
  arguments against this file.
-->
<sdf version="1.6">
  <world name="tunnel_test">
    <physics name="4ms" type="ignored">
      <max_step_size>0.004</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>
    <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-physics-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Physics">
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-scene-broadcaster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster">
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-user-commands-system" name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands">
    </plugin>
    <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-sensors-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors">
      <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>
    </plugin>

    <gui fullscreen="false">
      <plugin filename="MinimalScene" name="3D View">
        <ignition-gui>
          <title>3D View</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">docked</property>
        </ignition-gui>
        <engine>ogre2</engine>
        <scene>scene</scene>
        <ambient_light>0.4 0.4 0.4</ambient_light>
        <background_color>0.8 0.8 0.8</background_color>
        <camera_pose>-9 -8 8 0 0.5 0.6</camera_pose>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="GzSceneManager" name="Scene Manager">
        <ignition-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </ignition-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="InteractiveViewControl" name="Interactive view control">
        <ignition-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </ignition-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="CameraTracking" name="Camera Tracking">
        <ignition-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </ignition-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="WorldControl" name="World control">
        <ignition-gui>
          <title>World control</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">72</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">121</property>
          <property type="double" key="z">1</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="left" target="left"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </ignition-gui>
        <play_pause>true</play_pause>
        <step>true</step>
        <start_paused>false</start_paused>
        <use_event>true</use_event>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="WorldStats" name="World stats">
        <ignition-gui>
          <title>World stats</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">110</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">290</property>
          <property type="double" key="z">1</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="right" target="right"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </ignition-gui>
        <sim_time>true</sim_time>
        <real_time>true</real_time>
        <real_time_factor>true</real_time_factor>
        <iterations>true</iterations>
      </plugin>
    </gui>

    <light type="directional" name="sun">
      <!-- z=500 - see this file's top docstring / room_maze.world's own
           docstring for the real depth-camera-misreads-a-light bug this avoids. -->
      <cast_shadows>true</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 500 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <attenuation>
        <range>1000</range>
        <constant>0.9</constant>
        <linear>0.01</linear>
        <quadratic>0.001</quadratic>
      </attenuation>
      <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>
    </light>

    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>100 100</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>100 100</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.33 0.42 0.18 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.45 0.55 0.25 1</diffuse>
            <specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Outer room: x in [-6,6], y in [-4,4]. Same wall construction as
         room_maze.world (box collision+visual, plain ambient/diffuse color
         instead of a Classic-only material script). -->
    <model name="tunnel_room">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="wall_north">
        <pose>0 4 1.25 0 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>12.15 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>12.15 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="wall_south">
        <pose>0 -4 1.25 0 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>12.15 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>12.15 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="wall_east">
        <pose>6 0 1.25 0 0 1.5708</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>8 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>8 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="wall_west">
        <pose>-6 0 1.25 0 0 1.5708</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>8 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>8 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>

      <!-- Partition wall at x=0, split around the y in [-0.7, 0.7] gap the
           tunnel plugs (see top docstring - 0.7m is the tunnel arch's own
           radius, so these meet it flush with no leftover opening). -->
      <link name="partition_north">
        <!-- Spans y in [0.7, 4]: length 3.3, centered at y=2.35. -->
        <pose>0 2.35 1.25 0 0 1.5708</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>3.3 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>3.3 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.6 0.6 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.6 0.6 0.6 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="partition_south">
        <!-- Spans y in [-4, -0.7]: length 3.3, centered at y=-2.35. -->
        <pose>0 -2.35 1.25 0 0 1.5708</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>3.3 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>3.3 0.15 2.5</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.6 0.6 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.6 0.6 0.6 1</diffuse><specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- The tunnel: 7 flat box segments approximating a semicircular arch
         of radius 0.7m, extruded 1.5m along X (open at x=-0.75/+0.75 - the
         two mouths). Per-segment pose = (0, R*cos(theta_i), R*sin(theta_i),
         theta_i - 90deg, 0, 0) - see this file's top docstring for the
         derivation. Segment width 0.349m (chord 0.312m x ~1.12 overlap
         factor) so neighboring segments overlap slightly rather than
         leaving a seam. Distinct dark material so it visually reads as a
         separate structure (a culvert), not just "more wall". -->
    <model name="tunnel">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="arch_segment_0">
        <pose>0 0.6824 0.1558 -1.34640 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_1">
        <pose>0 0.5473 0.4364 -0.89760 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_2">
        <pose>0 0.3037 0.6307 -0.44880 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_3">
        <!-- The very top of the arch (theta=90deg, roll=0) - the segment
             directly under the UAV when it flies straight over the tunnel. -->
        <pose>0 0 0.7 0 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_4">
        <pose>0 -0.3037 0.6307 0.44880 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_5">
        <pose>0 -0.5473 0.4364 0.89760 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
      <link name="arch_segment_6">
        <pose>0 -0.6824 0.1558 1.34640 0 0</pose>
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>1.5 0.349 0.05</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.25 0.22 0.18 1</ambient><diffuse>0.3 0.27 0.22 1</diffuse><specular>0.1 0.1 0.1 1</specular></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Start marker (green) - matches the UGV's own spawn pose below
         exactly. Visual-only: no <collision> at all, so nothing (camera,
         lidar, or the robots themselves) can ever treat it as a real
         obstacle.

         REAL BUG FOUND LIVE: an earlier version of this marker was a 1m-TALL
         cylinder (radius 0.25, length 1.0, centered at z=0.5). Having no
         <collision> only means the PHYSICS engine ignores it - the depth
         CAMERA still renders it like any other visible geometry, and
         happily reports its TOP surface (z=1.0) as "the ground" to
         everything below it. Confirmed live: `/elevation_map` read
         elevation~1.0 at both markers' exact (x,y), even though the real
         ground there is flat at z=0 - a tall marker isn't just a visual
         aid, it's an undetected fake 1m obstacle from the mapping
         pipeline's point of view. Fixed by flattening it to a thin disc
         (length=0.02, resting essentially flush with the ground) - still
         clearly visible from the GUI/top-down view as a bright colored
         circle, but only a 2cm bump (well under compute_traversability's
         own max_step=0.15 threshold), so it reads as flat/EASY terrain
         instead of a fake tower - the same class of bug as emap's own
         step11 "a light posed inside the operational volume gets misread
         as geometry by this environment's software-rendered depth camera". -->
    <model name="start_marker">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-3.0 0.0 0.01 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.35</radius><length>0.02</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0 1 0 0.9</ambient>
            <diffuse>0 1 0 0.9</diffuse>
            <emissive>0 0.6 0 1</emissive>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- Goal marker (red) - matches waypoint_follower's goal_x/goal_y
         launch arguments for this demo exactly (see launch/tunnel_demo.launch.py).
         Same flattened-disc fix as start_marker above. -->
    <model name="goal_marker">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>3.0 0.0 0.01 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.35</radius><length>0.02</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>1 0 0 0.9</ambient>
            <diffuse>1 0 0 0.9</diffuse>
            <emissive>0.6 0 0 1</emissive>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <include>
      <name>iris_quad</name>
      <uri>model://iris_quad</uri>
      <!-- Near-ground spawn (see room_maze.world's own docstring for the
           real free-fall/tip-over bug this convention avoids) - room A
           side, but offset 1.5m in Y from the UGV's own spawn point below.

           REAL BUG FOUND LIVE: an earlier version of this file spawned the
           UAV at the EXACT same (x, y) as the UGV (both at (-3.0, 0.0)) -
           the two robots' collision geometry physically overlapped at
           spawn, and the resulting contact impulse tipped the UAV over
           (confirmed live: its odometry orientation quaternion read
           roughly (x=0.97, y=-0.18, z=0.16, w=0.02) - a huge roll, not a
           level hover - while `/cmd_vel` kept commanding a normal climb
           the whole time; a rolled-over multirotor's thrust axis no longer
           points anywhere near "up", so no amount of correct control logic
           could recover it, same class of bug as room_maze.world's own
           z=3.5-spawn free-fall issue, just triggered by a different root
           cause). Fixed by simply not spawning two robots on top of each
           other - 1.5m of clearance in Y is comfortably more than either
           robot's own footprint. -->
      <pose>-3.0 1.5 0.1 0 0 0</pose>

      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-multicopter-motor-model-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
        <robotNamespace>iris_quad</robotNamespace>
        <jointName>rotor_0_joint</jointName>
        <linkName>rotor_0</linkName>
        <turningDirection>ccw</turningDirection>
        <timeConstantUp>0.0125</timeConstantUp>
        <timeConstantDown>0.025</timeConstantDown>
        <maxRotVelocity>1100</maxRotVelocity>
        <motorConstant>5.84e-06</motorConstant>
        <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
        <commandSubTopic>gazebo/command/motor_speed</commandSubTopic>
        <motorNumber>0</motorNumber>
        <rotorDragCoefficient>0.000175</rotorDragCoefficient>
        <rollingMomentCoefficient>1e-06</rollingMomentCoefficient>
        <motorSpeedPubTopic>motor_speed/0</motorSpeedPubTopic>
        <rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>10</rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>
        <motorType>velocity</motorType>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-multicopter-motor-model-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
        <robotNamespace>iris_quad</robotNamespace>
        <jointName>rotor_1_joint</jointName>
        <linkName>rotor_1</linkName>
        <turningDirection>ccw</turningDirection>
        <timeConstantUp>0.0125</timeConstantUp>
        <timeConstantDown>0.025</timeConstantDown>
        <maxRotVelocity>1100</maxRotVelocity>
        <motorConstant>5.84e-06</motorConstant>
        <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
        <commandSubTopic>gazebo/command/motor_speed</commandSubTopic>
        <motorNumber>1</motorNumber>
        <rotorDragCoefficient>0.000175</rotorDragCoefficient>
        <rollingMomentCoefficient>1e-06</rollingMomentCoefficient>
        <motorSpeedPubTopic>motor_speed/1</motorSpeedPubTopic>
        <rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>10</rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>
        <motorType>velocity</motorType>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-multicopter-motor-model-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
        <robotNamespace>iris_quad</robotNamespace>
        <jointName>rotor_2_joint</jointName>
        <linkName>rotor_2</linkName>
        <turningDirection>cw</turningDirection>
        <timeConstantUp>0.0125</timeConstantUp>
        <timeConstantDown>0.025</timeConstantDown>
        <maxRotVelocity>1100</maxRotVelocity>
        <motorConstant>5.84e-06</motorConstant>
        <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
        <commandSubTopic>gazebo/command/motor_speed</commandSubTopic>
        <motorNumber>2</motorNumber>
        <rotorDragCoefficient>0.000175</rotorDragCoefficient>
        <rollingMomentCoefficient>1e-06</rollingMomentCoefficient>
        <motorSpeedPubTopic>motor_speed/2</motorSpeedPubTopic>
        <rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>10</rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>
        <motorType>velocity</motorType>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-multicopter-motor-model-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterMotorModel">
        <robotNamespace>iris_quad</robotNamespace>
        <jointName>rotor_3_joint</jointName>
        <linkName>rotor_3</linkName>
        <turningDirection>cw</turningDirection>
        <timeConstantUp>0.0125</timeConstantUp>
        <timeConstantDown>0.025</timeConstantDown>
        <maxRotVelocity>1100</maxRotVelocity>
        <motorConstant>5.84e-06</motorConstant>
        <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
        <commandSubTopic>gazebo/command/motor_speed</commandSubTopic>
        <motorNumber>3</motorNumber>
        <rotorDragCoefficient>0.000175</rotorDragCoefficient>
        <rollingMomentCoefficient>1e-06</rollingMomentCoefficient>
        <motorSpeedPubTopic>motor_speed/3</motorSpeedPubTopic>
        <rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>10</rotorVelocitySlowdownSim>
        <motorType>velocity</motorType>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-multicopter-control-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::MulticopterVelocityControl">
        <robotNamespace>iris_quad</robotNamespace>
        <commandSubTopic>gazebo/command/twist</commandSubTopic>
        <enableSubTopic>enable</enableSubTopic>
        <comLinkName>base_link</comLinkName>
        <velocityGain>2.7 2.7 2.7</velocityGain>
        <attitudeGain>2 3 0.15</attitudeGain>
        <angularRateGain>0.4 0.52 0.18</angularRateGain>
        <maximumLinearAcceleration>2 2 2</maximumLinearAcceleration>
        <rotorConfiguration>
          <rotor>
            <jointName>rotor_0_joint</jointName>
            <forceConstant>5.84e-06</forceConstant>
            <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
            <direction>1</direction>
          </rotor>
          <rotor>
            <jointName>rotor_1_joint</jointName>
            <forceConstant>5.84e-06</forceConstant>
            <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
            <direction>1</direction>
          </rotor>
          <rotor>
            <jointName>rotor_2_joint</jointName>
            <forceConstant>5.84e-06</forceConstant>
            <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
            <direction>-1</direction>
          </rotor>
          <rotor>
            <jointName>rotor_3_joint</jointName>
            <forceConstant>5.84e-06</forceConstant>
            <momentConstant>0.06</momentConstant>
            <direction>-1</direction>
          </rotor>
        </rotorConfiguration>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-odometry-publisher-system"
        name="ignition::gazebo::systems::OdometryPublisher">
        <dimensions>3</dimensions>
        <odom_frame>iris_quad/odom</odom_frame>
        <robot_base_frame>iris_quad/base_link</robot_base_frame>
      </plugin>
    </include>

    <!-- The UGV - spawns at the green marker's (x, y): room A, aligned with
         the tunnel's own centerline (y=0) so the straight-line path to the
         goal genuinely passes through the tunnel, not just near it. MUST
         match launch/tunnel_demo.launch.py's ugv_odom_static_tf translation
         exactly - same single-source-of-truth convention room_maze.world
         and nav_sim.launch.py already use for nav_ugv's spawn pose. -->
    <include>
      <name>nav_ugv</name>
      <uri>model://nav_ugv</uri>
      <pose>-3.0 0.0 0.0 0 0 0</pose>

      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-diff-drive-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::DiffDrive">
        <left_joint>left_wheel_joint</left_joint>
        <right_joint>right_wheel_joint</right_joint>
        <wheel_separation>0.4</wheel_separation>
        <wheel_radius>0.05</wheel_radius>
        <topic>cmd_vel</topic>
        <odom_topic>odometry</odom_topic>
        <!-- REAL BUG FOUND LIVE (GUI-mode run, 2026-09-24): this plugin's
             OWN odom/TF output (frame_id/child_frame_id below) is DEAD-
             RECKONED from wheel rotation, not the chassis's true simulated
             position - see this project's own "wheel odometry lied"
             retraction in docs/work-docs/nav/step06_hybrid_3d_voxel_
             navigation.md. Confirmed live: after a chassis-stability event
             (now separately fixed - see models/nav_ugv/model.sdf's
             front_caster_wheel), this dead-reckoned odom diverged from
             Ignition's own physics ground truth (`/world/tunnel_test/
             dynamic_pose/info`) by SEVERAL METERS while the robot was
             mid-drive - not a one-time freeze, an ongoing drift under
             normal turning. Renamed to its own dedicated, UNUSED frame
             pair so it's obviously not what anything else in this system
             trusts for localization (kept publishing at all only for
             manual diagnostic comparison against ground truth, e.g. while
             debugging exactly this class of bug again in the future) -
             the REAL nav_ugv/odom -> nav_ugv/base_link TF pair (the one
             bridge.yaml actually bridges to ROS `/tf`, and everything
             else - Nav2's costmaps, waypoint_follower's TF lookups,
             bt_navigator's own position tracking - relies on) now comes
             from the OdometryPublisher plugin below instead, exactly
             mirroring iris_quad's own already-correct pattern (see
             emap/worlds/bump_test.world's own OdometryPublisher block and
             its bridge.yaml's "/model/iris_quad/pose" comment) - ground
             truth, not wheel integration. -->
        <frame_id>nav_ugv/wheel_odom</frame_id>
        <child_frame_id>nav_ugv/wheel_odom_base</child_frame_id>
        <odom_publish_frequency>30</odom_publish_frequency>
      </plugin>

      <!-- Ground-truth odom/TF (see the DiffDrive plugin's own comment
           above for the full story of why this exists) - same plugin,
           same 2-parameter shape, same reasoning as iris_quad's own block
           (emap/worlds/bump_test.world), just <dimensions>2</dimensions>
           since nav_ugv is a planar ground vehicle, not a 3D flyer. Odom
           frame naming (nav_ugv/odom) is unchanged from before this fix -
           the existing ugv_odom_static_tf static transform (iris_quad/odom
           -> nav_ugv/odom, -3,0,0 - see launch/tunnel_demo.launch.py) still
           composes correctly on top of it, confirmed live: this plugin
           resets to (0,0,0) at the model's own spawn pose, exactly like
           DiffDrive's own odom convention did, so the existing offset's
           meaning ("distance since spawn" -> "absolute world position")
           is unchanged - only the SOURCE of that distance is now accurate. -->
      <plugin filename="ignition-gazebo-odometry-publisher-system"
        name="gz::sim::systems::OdometryPublisher">
        <dimensions>2</dimensions>
        <odom_frame>nav_ugv/odom</odom_frame>
        <robot_base_frame>nav_ugv/base_link</robot_base_frame>
        <odom_publish_frequency>30</odom_publish_frequency>
      </plugin>
    </include>

    <!-- Static overhead overview camera capturing the complete room (with tunnel).
         REFRAMED (2026-09-24, user report: "wider view which captures all
         elements in the room"): the room's own real outer-wall footprint is
         ~12m x 8m (side walls at x=+/-6, front/back walls at y=+/-4 - see
         tunnel_room's own wall poses/sizes above). The original z=10.5m
         gave an 18.5m x 13.9m ground footprint at this hfov - the room only
         filled about 65% of the frame's width, leaving a large wasted gray
         margin and making every element (robots, markers, tunnel) smaller
         and harder to make out than necessary. Lowered to z=7.65m for a
         ~13.5m x 10.1m footprint - the room now fills almost the entire
         frame with a small clean margin, same hfov/pitch (still straight
         down, still the whole room, nothing newly cropped out - the room
         is only 8m tall at its walls, well inside this footprint).
         Resolution was briefly doubled to 1280x960 for extra clarity, but
         that was found live to be the wrong tradeoff: it quadrupled this
         single camera's render cost and dropped its actual achieved rate
         from several Hz down to ~0.6Hz (a new frame every ~1.6s) under
         this sandbox's CPU-bound rendering - choppier, not clearer, in the
         final video. Reverted to 640x480 (unchanged); the height/FOV
         reframing above is the real, load-free clarity win. -->
    <model name="overhead_overview_camera">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0 7.65 0 1.5707963 1.5707963</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <sensor name="room_overview_camera" type="camera">
          <always_on>true</always_on>
          <update_rate>15</update_rate>
          <visualize>true</visualize>
          <topic>/room_overhead/image</topic>
          <camera>
            <horizontal_fov>1.45</horizontal_fov>
            <image>
              <width>640</width>
              <height>480</height>
            </image>
            <clip>
              <near>0.1</near>
              <far>100</far>
            </clip>
          </camera>
        </sensor>
      </link>
    </model>
  </world>
</sdf>
